{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact head 5eb4e8b756ed46986cb73f87109f31372ea6a849, signing the complete six-artifact set: 17afb9de internal/kernel (primary), 030a6554 internal/app, d4a82aa4 cmd/gs, 6aad7f97 docs, bbada818 cmd/gitseq-mcp, 740b5979 internal/service. This closes audit 9190ffe8 at sequence 5288, which recorded the same finding I had reached independently: the head changes six maintained paths and only four were authorized. It reuses no withdrawn review as authority. My own durable record of the previous round, including the evidence reproduced below, is assert a12e0d2f.\n\nTHE HEAD IS UNCHANGED. Worktree HEAD, the local branch and origin all read 5eb4e8b7 and the worktree is clean. Nothing has moved since the round whose evidence I carry forward, so that evidence still describes this commit.\n\nALL SIX ARTIFACTS CHECKED, ONE BY ONE. Each resolves in the projection, none is retired, every one reads stale:false, every one names commit 5eb4e8b7 exactly, and every one is authored by the implementer 5f12e916, which is what reviewedPaths requires of a citation before it counts. The two new ones cover exactly the two paths my finding named, cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/service, and no others.\n\nTHE SET NOW SPANS THE HEAD, AND I CHECKED THAT MECHANICALLY RATHER THAN BY EYE. Reducing `git diff --name-only main..5eb4e8b7` to maintained areas gives exactly six: cmd/gitseq-mcp, cmd/gs, docs, internal/app, internal/kernel, internal/service. I then took every live artifact in the projection and kept those whose path covers a changed file. Every one of them falls under one of the six signed strings; there is no wider pointer at `internal` or `cmd` that the wider-path rule would make win instead. One case deserves naming because it is easy to miss: a live artifact stands at the narrower path internal/kernel/kernel_test.go, event 5feb6070, and it is mine rather than the implementer's. The head changes that file, so the merge must retire it. It is reached, because